    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved every registration-date\u2013derived value onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year = 1 July \u2192 30 June, labelled by the calendar year it *ends* in, so `2026-09-04 \u2192 FY27`).\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `endingYear(date)` \u2014 the calendar year the fiscal year ends in (month \u2265 July \u2192 year+1).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` string (null-safe).\n- `elapsedBetween(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed (count of 1 July boundaries crossed).\n\n**Behaviour changes (per spec):**\n1. **`fiscalYear` response field** \u2014 added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` and wired into `OwnerMapper` as a read-time computed mapping `FiscalYear.label(owner.getRegistrationDate())`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `\"fiscalYear\": \"FY27\"`.\n2. **Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` now uses the fiscal-year two digits instead of the calendar year (`\u2026-M27` rather than `\u2026-M26` for a September 2026 date).\n3. **Tenure** \u2014 `AssignMembershipLevel` now scores its 3 points when tenure exceeds **one elapsed fiscal year** (`FiscalYear.elapsedBetween`), replacing the old strict 365-day window.\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions for `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, and the JavaDoc on the two functions to match.\n\n**Convention note:** the spec fixes the 1 July start and the `FY<YY>` format but not whether `YY` is the starting or ending year. I chose the dominant convention (label = ending year), which the `FY\\d{2}` test accepts either way; both the `fiscalYear` field and the membership number derive from the same `FiscalYear.endingYear`, so they stay consistent. The audit log confirmed `registrationDate=2026-09-04 \u2192 membershipNumber=\u2026-M27`.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
